{"id": "EUVD-2026-103310", "enisaUuid": "e3e099a3-5114-3a49-9528-cb575409c756", "description": "phpMyFAQ before 4.1.9 and 4.2.0-alpha before 4.2.0-beta contains an authorization bypass vulnerability in attachment.php that allows attackers to download attachments of restricted FAQs by bypassing per-record permission checks. Low-privileged users with the dlattachment right, or anonymous users when allowDownloadsForGuests is enabled, can request attachment IDs to retrieve confidential files from restricted FAQs.", "datePublished": "2026-10-17T18:46:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T21:41:44", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/thorsten/phpMyFAQ/security/advisories/GHSA-pp67-9fv9-ph7q", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/phpmyfaq-before-4.1.9-and-4.2.0-alpha-before-4.2.0-beta-authorization-bypass-via-attachment-php-downloads"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x6rh-6v24-8xcj", "CVE-2026-111910"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1297b22f-9af1-33c6-8e0d-a7e82b42799b", "product": {"name": "phpMyFAQ", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.1.9"}, {"id": "bc22ea75-e105-32d5-8d3c-668ea15eb52f", "product": {"name": "phpMyFAQ", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}, "product_version": "4.2.0-alpha <4.2.0-beta"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4b30d92c-3db8-3a7b-82a9-63d51de9a006", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}], "isExploited": false}